  "highlight": "James Pittar crossed the English Channel from England to France in 13 hours 50 minutes on 19 July 1998.",
  "biography": [
    "Pittar was 28 when he swam from England to France. He went on to become the first blind swimmer to complete the English Channel, Catalina and Manhattan combination, according to the International Marathon Swimming Hall of Fame, which inducted him in 2009.",
    "The English Channel swim on 19 July 1998 took 13 hours 50 minutes. The Catalina federation records 11 hours 36 minutes 50 seconds on 15 September 2006. In New York the 12 June 1999 Manhattan circuit took 7 hours 58 minutes 55 seconds."
